Title: The Last Customer
Credit: An original example for The Big Slop

INT. DINER - NIGHT

Rain needles the windows of an empty roadside diner. A jukebox plays to nobody.

MARA, a waitress in a faded yellow uniform, wipes the same spot on the counter. A small brass bell sits beside the register.

The door opens. ELI enters, carrying a battered red suitcase.

MARA
We're closed.

ELI
Your sign says open.

MARA
The sign's an optimist.

He puts the suitcase on a stool. Something inside it rings.

ELI
Just a coffee. And maybe some advice.

Mara looks at the suitcase. Then at the brass bell.

MARA
Coffee's two dollars. Advice depends on what's in the bag.

EXT. DINER - NIGHT

The neon sign flickers. For one moment, the rain falls upward.

FADE OUT.
